=== .claude/rules/forge-secrets.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Secrets. Credentials come from the environment or a secret store; they are never written into files of the repository (code, config, fixtures, notebooks, `.env.example`).
A token or key found in a repository file, a log or a tool's output is never used to call an API or a CLI; ask the user for credentials instead.
Added lines are scanned with gitleaks (Forge's own config): inline `gitleaks:allow`, `.gitleaksignore` and a project `.gitleaks.toml` do not silence it.
Keystores, private keys and auth files (`*.p12`, `*.pfx`, `*.jks`, `*.key`, `id_rsa`, `.pypirc`, `.netrc`, `.git-credentials`) are not committed; `.npmrc` tokens are `${NPM_TOKEN}`-style references.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-pnpm.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

pnpm is the package manager: `pnpm add`, `pnpm install`; npm, yarn and bun installs ask.
pnpm settings (overrides, allowBuilds, minimumReleaseAge, nodeLinker, …) go in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`; a `pnpm` field in package.json and pnpm settings in `.npmrc` (registry and auth only) are rejected.
pnpm 11: `allowBuilds` replaces `onlyBuiltDependencies` / `neverBuiltDependencies` / `ignoredBuiltDependencies` / `ignoreDepScripts`, `allowUnusedPatches` replaces `allowNonAppliedPatches`, `auditConfig.ignoreGhsas` replaces `ignoreCves`.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-vitest.md
---
paths:
  - "packages/core/**"
---

These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Vitest 4. Several test setups are `test.projects` in `vitest.config.*`; a `vitest.workspace.*` file is ignored. Parallelism is set with `maxWorkers`.
Tests assert behaviour: never weaken, remove or skip an assertion to make a test pass.
When the task changes behaviour an existing test asserts, update that test in place with Edit or Write (keep its name; Forge asks for approval) and say so in your summary. Otherwise never edit an existing test to make the code pass.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript.md
---
paths:
  - "packages/core/**"
---

These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

TypeScript, strict.
TypeScript 6 deprecates `baseUrl`, `moduleResolution: "node10"`, `target: "es5"` and `esModuleInterop: false`, and TypeScript 7 removes them: migrate them; `ignoreDeprecations` in a tsconfig is rejected.
`!` non-null assertions and `as unknown as T` are rejected: narrow with a check, or parse with a schema.
Before writing a utility, search the codebase for an existing helper (warn-once and logging helpers, `util.*` functions such as an existing property setter) and reuse it instead of adding a near-duplicate.
Type-only imports and re-exports use `import type` / `export type`. `JSON.parse` and `res.json()` results stay `unknown` until a schema validates them; literals take `satisfies T` or an annotation, not `as T`.
=== .claude/settings.json
{
  "permissions": {
    "ask": [
      "Edit(.forge/**)",
      "Edit(forge.yaml)",
      "Edit(forge.lock)",
      "Edit(.claude/rules/forge-*.md)",
      "Edit(**/biome.json)",
      "Edit(**/biome.jsonc)",
      "Edit(**/tsconfig*.json)",
      "Edit(**/eslint.config.*)",
      "Edit(**/.oxlintrc.json)",
      "Edit(**/deno.json)",
      "Edit(**/deno.jsonc)",
      "Edit(**/.prettierrc*)",
      "Edit(**/prettier.config.*)",
      "Edit(**/pnpm-workspace.yaml)",
      "Edit(**/.npmrc)",
      "Edit(**/.yarnrc.yml)",
      "Edit(**/bunfig.toml)",
      "Edit(**/turbo.json)",
      "Edit(**/vitest.config.*)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf \"{\\\"systemMessage\\\":\\\"Forge is not installed, so this project\\047s checks are off. Install it with: curl -LsSf https://github.com/mde-pach/claude-forge/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh\\\"}\\n\"; exit 0; }; exec claude-forge hook session-start'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook user-prompt-submit'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180,
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read|Edit|Write|Grep|Glob|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-failure'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook stop'",
            "timeout": 600
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PermissionRequest": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook permission-request'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook session-end'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
